-- title:
--   Ordinarity at p descends along a jointly injective family of local points
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a commutative local ring and let $A_0,\dots,A_{n-1}$ be a finite family of commutative local rings indexed by `Fin n`, equipped with ring homomorphisms $\chi_i : P \to A_i$ each of which is local (non-units go to non-units), and assume the family is jointly injective: if $\chi_i(x)=0$ for every $i$ then $x=0$. Let $\rho$ be an element of [`GaloisRepAdic P`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is a $P$-module $V$, free and finite with $\operatorname{rank}_P V = 2$, together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb Q$) to $\mathrm{End}_P(V)$ which is $\mathfrak m_P$-adically continuous, in the sense that for each $m$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak m_P^m \cdot V$ for all $v$. Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and assume `DetIsCyclotomic`: $p \in \mathfrak m_P$ and, for all $m$, all $\sigma$ and all $a \in \mathbb N$ such that $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for every $p^m$-th root of unity $\mu$, one has $\det \rho(\sigma) \equiv a$ modulo the ideal generated by $p^m$ in $P$. Assume finally that for each $i$ the base change of $\rho$ along $\chi_i$, namely $A_i \otimes_P V$ with $\sigma$ acting by $\mathrm{id} \otimes \rho(\sigma)$, is ordinary at $p$. Then $\rho$ itself is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring $\mathcal O$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $\mathcal O$ there is a $P$-submodule $L \subseteq V$ of the form $P \cdot b_0$ for some $P$-basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $V$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $\mathcal O$ over $\mathbb Q$, and such that $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $v \in V$ and all $\sigma$ in the image in the decomposition subgroup of the inertia subgroup of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the gluing step for the ordinary local condition: ordinarity of a two-dimensional $\mathfrak m$-adic representation over a local ring can be checked after specialising along any finite family of local points that separates the elements of the ring. It is used in the construction of Hecke–Galois representation data attached to cusp forms, where the relevant ring is detected by finitely many of its local quotients.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_isOrdinaryAt_of_forall_point.lean

